  "answer": "The study confirmed five settings on five different scenes where the policy fails in most runs. Four of them move the other cars earlier: 09a95ffa at -2 s and 1.5x (S10), 023b7fcc at -2 s and 2x (S1), 0e899dd3 at -1.5 s and 2x (S19) and 054b5901 at -1.5 s and 0.75x (S3). The fifth is 19f339ba at +0.5 s and the recorded speed (S26). Every kept run at these five settings failed. The 90% ranges for most of them only just clear one half, though, so they are confirmed as likely failures but not ranked against each other. All the failures at S10 and S3 are flagged as possible simulator artifacts, because the ego was over 3.5 m from the recorded path. Triage still blames the policy in each case: it drifted left against a RIGHT route command, then either ran into a slower car ahead or drove onto a median. In all five scenes every car was retimed, not one marked cut-in car, so the study can't say which car's timing causes the failure.",
